<title>HUNGARY: Hungary twelve-month bill yield rises to 20.50 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary twelve-month bill yield rises to 20.50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of twelve-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 20.50 percent, up from 20.07 percent at an auction two weeks ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said. Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     15,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received	18,084.30 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    15,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 18,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    20.50 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     83.1038 pct</p>
</text>
